    { tag: "stretch", q: "Synthesise the entire builder phase: an agent is reliable (10.5) AND secure (10.6) AND economical (9.7) AND well-architected (10.2) — explain how these four disciplines relate, why an agent needs ALL of them to be truly deployable, and why this combination is a rare and valuable skill.",
      sol: "<b>How they relate:</b> ARCHITECTURE (10.2) decides the agent's shape (which patterns, where autonomy) — the foundation. RELIABILITY (10.5) makes it work dependably on real input (evals, guardrails, human-in-the-loop, observability). SECURITY (10.6) makes it safe against adversaries (trifecta broken, sandboxed, least-privilege, hinged). ECONOMICS (9.7) makes it profitable (model mix, caching, loop limits). They're INTERDEPENDENT: a well-architected but unreliable agent fails in production; a reliable but insecure one is a breach; a secure but uneconomical one loses money; an economical but poorly-architected one solves the wrong problem. <b>Why all four are needed:</b> a truly deployable agent must WORK (reliability), not be EXPLOITABLE (security), not LOSE MONEY (economics), and SOLVE THE RIGHT PROBLEM the right way (architecture) — miss any one and it's not deployable, just a demo with a hidden flaw. <b>Why the combination is rare and valuable:</b> most builders master ONE dimension. The person who holds ALL FOUR — can architect an agent, make it reliable, secure it against adversaries, AND make it profitable — is exactly who companies desperately need to deploy AI they can depend on, and almost nobody is. That's the design of this course: nine tracks built each discipline precisely so that here, at the summit, you can COMPOSE them into deployable autonomous systems — the single most valuable, most trusted, most premium capability in applied AI. This composition IS your competitive moat and market position, and it's what Phase E converts into income. The builder phase doesn't end with 'you can build agents'; it ends with 'you can build agents people can actually trust with real stakes' — which is the whole game, and now it's yours." }
